          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "త్వరగా (tvaragā) — \"quickly\", and at a parting, \"soon\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "త్వరగా (tvaragā) రండి — \"come back soon\". The respectful raṇḍi you already have."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "త్వరగా (tvaragā) is Sanskrit tvarā, \"haste\", with the Telugu adverb ending -gā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An invitation to return, built from pieces you own."
